{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261111T181049Z-923e1f1b", "ts": "2026-11-11T18:15:06Z", "actor": {"worktree": "cordyceps", "plugin": "3.8.2-dev", "branch": "feature/edit-transaction", "build": "a278eb560a51"}, "body": {"base_commit": "e0759794642033479015bcb15817afa38a6a9dc7", "base_tree": "b242500dfce14ac6a6106caa2b4cdc30d0d23794", "head_tree": "46bed9006a1b2c0c782b9b2cb84eb7b76ac8c699", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "4212d60c59fb6150a2d159487e6b44de3144d42b", "mode": "final (full review, ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "inner", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["src/Cordyceps.Tests/Cordyceps.Tests.csproj", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/EditJournalTests.cs", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/EditRepliesTests.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditJournal.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditReplies.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/UndoEvents.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/GrasshopperContext.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Tools/Unified/GhWireTool.cs"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-edit-transaction.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/Cordyceps.Tests.csproj", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/EditJournalTests.cs", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/EditRepliesTests.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditJournal.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditReplies.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/UndoEvents.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/GrasshopperContext.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Tools/Unified/GhWireTool.cs"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-edit-transaction.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md"], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Chunk 01's 'forced failure after the first wire' criterion, and VRF-024's 'after a forced rollback' step, have no way to force a failure in the host", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Once validation passes, no gh_wire body can fail, and nothing in src/ can inject a fault into EditTransaction.Run (a search for forced-rollback or fault-injection hooks finds only the plan's own wording). So the acceptance criterion is shown only at the journal level, by the fake-sink tests Rollback_UndoesNewestFirst and Rollback_CarriesOnPastFailingActions. VRF-024's per-family 'archive after forced rollback' comparison cannot be run as written for gh_wire, or for any family whose body has no failure path. Before Chunk 06 writes VRF-024, either plan a fault hook (for example a Release-safe debug switch read by EditTransaction.Run that throws after the Nth recorder call) or reword the criterion and the VRF step to say the logic is proven by the journal tests and the host check covers only Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Shift+Z.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Tools/Unified/GhWireTool.cs"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "EditTransaction.Run's routing decisions are untested host logic", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. These decisions live in host-coupled EditTransaction.Run, which the test project does not link: a nested edit of the same document joins the open one; one of another document throws; EditRollbackException is answered as refused and anything else as unexpected; `undo` is set only when HasChanges; `solve` is set only on a refusal. The journal and the reply shapes are well tested. This routing is not, and the join and other-document branches are not reached until batch (#96). CLAUDE.md says 'New decision logic goes in a host-free Core/ file linked into Cordyceps.Tests, with tests'. Consider moving the routing into a host-free piece (for example a static Run<TDoc> over the journal and EditReplies) so those branches get tests before Chunk 02 onward depends on them.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "A throw from Commit escapes after the edit is already applied", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. In Run, `tx._journal.Commit()` sits outside the try/catch that handles rollback, and Commit sets its phase to Committed before EndApply, Push, Expire and ScheduleSolve run. If PushUndoRecord, an ExpireSolution, or SolveCoordinator.Schedule throws, the mutations stay with no undo record (or with one), and the call answers with whatever the MCP layer makes of the exception. That reads as a failed call whose changes persisted, which is the half-edited outcome the plan's Product goal excludes. It is unlikely, since these are host calls that rarely throw. Consider catching around Commit and answering success with a warning field (the edit happened), or at least logging it with the record name.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "Contributor instructions still teach mutation outside the edit layer, and no chunk plans the update", "recommendation": "CLAUDE.md's 'Rules for code changes' and 'Adding or modifying tools' template (return _context.ExecuteOnUiThread(() => { ... mutate ... })) and docs/architecture.md line 17 name ExecuteOnUiThread as the document-access path. None of them mentions _context.Edit. The plan's Architecture goal says every mutating call runs inside one EditTransaction, because one unrecorded edit breaks Ctrl+Z for the recorded ones (modal 'undo failed'). Chunk 06's audit list leaves out CLAUDE.md and docs/architecture.md. Once the branch lands, a new action written from the template recreates the mixed state. Class fix: add CLAUDE.md and docs/architecture.md to Chunk 06's deliverables, and make the template mutate through _context.Edit(doc, EditReplies.RecordName(tool, action), tx => ...) with record-before-mutate.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/GrasshopperContext.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Journal marks Committed before the push and solve run, so a commit-time throw has no modelled outcome", "recommendation": "EditJournal.Commit sets _phase = Committed before it calls EndApply, Push, Expire and ScheduleSolve. EditTransaction.Run calls Commit outside its try/catch. If Push throws (or SolveCoordinator.Schedule does, for example inside SolutionWatcher.EnsureWatched), the exception escapes Run with no reply shape. The document stays mutated, and either no undo record exists (the unrecorded-edit state the plan forbids) or a record was pushed but the call reports failure, which invites a retry. Instance fix: decide which of these is the post-commit contract and encode it. One option is to set Committed only after Push and catch a post-push scheduling failure into the committed reply. The other is to roll back when Push throws.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditJournal.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "'Was a record pushed' is derived twice: Commit's actions.Count and Run's HasChanges", "recommendation": "Commit decides whether to push from actions.Count > 0. Run separately recomputes journal.HasChanges to decide whether the reply carries undo. The two agree today only because Commit drops pending entries before counting. Have Commit return what it did (pushed, scheduled) and build the reply from that, so the undo field cannot drift from the push. This is a borderline case (two signals, localized), so it is an observation. Instance.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditJournal.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Rollback expires survivors unconditionally but schedules only when entries exist, unlike Commit", "recommendation": "Commit schedules when actions.Count > 0 || _expire.Count > 0. Rollback always expires survivors but schedules only when _entries.Count > 0. A body that calls tx.Expire, records nothing and then throws leaves those objects expired with no solve scheduled, so outputs and previews stay stale until something else solves. Nothing in Chunk 01 calls tx.Expire, so the case is unreachable today. Instance fix: use one condition for both paths (schedule iff anything was expired), and pin it with an Expire-only rollback test next to Rollback_WithNothingRecorded_RestoresTheDocumentAndSchedulesNothing.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditJournal.cs"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "EditJournal.Add cannot express a refused add, so a refused add is captured and later undone as if it happened", "recommendation": "The journal's Add takes an Action, so EditTransaction.AddObject learns Document.AddObject returned false only after journal.Add has already captured CreateAddObjectEvent and marked the entry non-pending. The EditRollbackException thrown next then rolls back by Undo-ing an add of an object that was never inserted. That turns a clean refusal into a possible rollback failure ('Check the canvas'). If GH_AddObjectAction's undo resolves by InstanceGuid, it could also remove the pre-existing object whose id collided, which is the case the refusal message names. Throw inside the add delegate instead, or make Add take a Func<bool>, so a refused add stays Pending and RemoveAdded's reference check governs. Chunk 03 is the first caller; settle it before then. Instance.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditJournal.cs"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Edit replies are re-serialized through a default Newtonsoft parse that reinterprets date-shaped strings, so the MCP reply contract can change silently", "recommendation": "EditReplies.ParseBody calls JToken.Parse(body) with Newtonsoft's defaults (DateParseHandling.DateTime), and EditReplies.Committed then emits body.ToString(). Every migrated tool's reply goes through this round-trip. A string that looks like a date (a NickName such as \"2026-08-21T12:00:00+02:00\" or one with fractional seconds, both carried in gh_wire connect's source/target `name`) becomes a DateTime and comes back out in a different form, converted to the local offset or with the fraction dropped. The plan's norm disposition says response shapes are kept and gain only `undo`, and the MCP Tool/Action Contract in boundary-patterns.md calls the JSON response shape breaking, but nothing shows the cost of re-serializing was looked at. The codebase has already solved this twice: ParseHelpers.ParseJsonKeepingText, and StatusEnvelope.ParsePreservingText, which StatusEnvelopeTests.Inject_DoesNotReinterpretDateLikeStrings pins. ParseBody bypasses both. That is the learnings rule \"Tracing consumers of a shared helper misses paths that bypass it\". Scope: instance with one owner. ParseBody is the single place every edit reply passes through, and McpResultFormatter.IsErrorResult is the only other default parse in src/Cordyceps, and it only reads. Fix: parse through ParseHelpers.ParseJsonKeepingText (DateParseHandling.None) and add an EditRepliesTests fidelity test that asserts on the emitted text, as the StatusEnvelope test does.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditReplies.cs", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/EditRepliesTests.cs"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "A failure after the body returns (commit, or the end of a rollback) is reported as a plain failed call, with no sign of whether the edit landed", "recommendation": "In EditTransaction.Run, tx._journal.Commit() is outside the try/catch that handles the body. Commit removes pending adds, restores the solver, then calls Push, Expire and ScheduleSolve. If any of these throws, the exception leaves Run and reaches McpServer's tool-invocation boundary as a generic {success:false,error}, while the canvas changes stay. If Push itself threw, they stay with no undo record, which is the mixed recorded/unrecorded state the plan's Architecture goal says causes a modal undo-failed assert. The agent reads the call as failed and may retry, and nothing tells it to check the canvas. The rollback path has the same gap: a throw from ScheduleSolve, or from AfterRollback's canvas Invalidate, discards the RollbackReport, so the reply loses `rolledBack` and `rollbackFailures`. EditJournalTests has no sink whose Push or ScheduleSolve throws. Instance: guard the tail in Run. Before Push succeeds, roll back. After it, answer with the committed reply plus the solve error. Log either way. Add a fake-sink test for each case.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditJournal.cs"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "The new norm that every mutating call runs inside one EditTransaction has no durable home outside the build plan, and Chunk 06's doc list doesn't add one", "recommendation": "The plan's Architecture goal records why every call must go through the edit layer: an unrecorded edit breaks the preconditions of a recorded one, and Ctrl+Z then raises Grasshopper's modal undo-failed assert. That reasoning lives only in build-plan-edit-transaction.md, which gets archived. Two places tell a contributor how to write a tool, and neither mentions `_context.Edit`. CLAUDE.md's 'Rules for code changes' and its 'Adding or modifying tools' template show a direct mutation inside ExecuteOnUiThread. docs/architecture.md lists the Core modules (SolveCoordinator included) but not Core/Edits. Chunk 06's audit list names neither file. After merge, a contributor adding a mutating action will follow the CLAUDE.md template and recreate the mixed state. Instance: add a CLAUDE.md rule ('document mutations go through `_context.Edit`') and a docs/architecture.md entry for Core/Edits to Chunk 06's deliverables. Also consider turning Chunk 06's one-time 'grep finds no document mutation outside a transaction' acceptance check into a test, so the norm stays enforced.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/GrasshopperContext.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Edits/EditTransaction.cs"], "oid": "O-11"}], "duration_seconds": 540, "scope": "edit-transaction", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": "b242500dfce14ac6a6106caa2b4cdc30d0d23794", "chunks": ["01", "02"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-edit-transaction.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01", "02"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-edit-transaction.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-11T18:10:50Z"}}

